- `branch(b1, ...)`, `branch(b2, ...)`, `branch(b3, ...)`: Missing `guard` statements to encode the explicit conditions "If there is no suitable candidate available" and "if there is a suitable candidate available", leaving the XOR choice logic semantically undefined.
- `precedence(b1, n4)`: Routes the positive-availability path to another check node (`n4`) instead of advancing toward selection, contradicting the instruction that if a candidate is available, the process should "continue with the process" and "proceed with selecting".
- `precedence(n6, n10)`, `precedence(n10, e2)`: Creates a termination path immediately after "advertise the vacancy again", directly violating the constraint that "Once the candidate is appointed, the process comes to an end".
- `defines(v1, ...)`, `defines(v2, ...)`, `defines(v3, ...)`: Assign an empty range `{}` to decision variables representing candidate availability, failing to reflect the necessary boolean/value space for the stated yes/no conditions.
- `action(n10, "process ends")`, `end(e2)`: Hallucinated terminal constructs; the source specifies a single process endpoint triggered exclusively after appointment (`n8`), not after repeated advertising.

Structural Check
- [S1] STC9 failed: Each branch node must have exactly one incoming and at least two outgoing edges. | Node `b2` has in=1 and out=1. | DSL: branch(b2,XOR)
- [S2] STC11 failed: Each variable definition must have a valid range with at least two distinct values. | Variable `v1` has an invalid range `[]`. | Variable `v2` has an invalid range `[]`. | Variable `v3` has an invalid range `[]`.
- [S3] STC16 failed: Every outgoing edge of XOR/OR branches must have exactly one guard. | XOR/OR edge `b1 -> n3` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b1 -> n4` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b2 -> c1` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b3 -> n6` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b3 -> c1` has 0 guards; exactly one is required.